WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:07.040
Film Courage: I know you’re writing your
autobiography So I’m going to steal a question

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.040
I heard on C-Span.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.980
I just finished watching THE POST movie and
they interviewed Katharine Graham years ago

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:17.180
and she wrote a tell-all book about THE POST
and her family and the troubles with her husband

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.570
and his depression (things like that).

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:24.230
And the interviewer said t her “Why do you
want people to know this?”

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.060
She said “Good question.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.950
I started [writing] and I was only going to
tell one thing and I just kept going.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.590
I couldn’t stop.”

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:43.160
Bill Duke, Actor/Filmmaker/Author: I’m writing
this book

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:48.030
for all the losers in the world.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:53.680
For all the people who have been told you
cannot do it, you’re a loser, you’re too

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:58.100
stupid, you’re too ugly, you’re too dumb
or too black.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.420
You’re too whatever.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.870
You’re never going to make it.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:13.601
I’ve been called all those things 
and worse.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:19.440
I’m writing this book because I want children
who are going through similar things to never

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:22.190
give up on themselves.

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:24.531
If I can get through it so can you.

00:01:24.531 --> 00:01:35.890
Never…never…whether you are five or 100,
never give up.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:39.950
It’s never too late.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.660
You determine your reality.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:46.670
Are there forces that help shape the context
around you?

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:49.350
Of course there are.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:57.990
I mean…but what is your responsibility?

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.130
Because the boogeyman is bigger than you,
you don’t fight back?

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.240
You don’t do nothing?

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.440
You don’t bite his toe?

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:03.520
You don’t do nothing?

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:10.000
You just talk about the size of the boogeyman,
how long he’s been on your neck?

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:19.330
The color of the boogeyman, the boogeyman
system, how can I say?

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:22.520
The odor of his breath?

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:32.880
You can describe every aspect of the boogeyman
for the rest of your damn life or you can

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.780
bite his toe.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.810
Now you ain’t going to l him if you bite
his toe, but toe’s are sensitive.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:45.580
There’s going to be some movement.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:54.200
All you need is a little bit…a little bit…but
you’re not going to bite?

00:02:54.200 --> 00:03:00.120
That’s your definition of your possibilities
in life.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:07.530
“I can’t bite because the boogeyman is
so big and I’m so weak…goodbye.”

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.850
Sorry.

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:14.490
Not me.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:15.840
Not me.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.060
Never.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:34.950
You’ve got to have 
my guess a couple of, they better

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:48.819
hit something that is vital because they can
remove them and I’m coming back.

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:50.709
Never give up.

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:51.709
Never.

00:03:51.709 --> 00:04:03.260
And as my family used to say to the people
who try to stop you and put you down, there

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:12.170
is only one phrase that they deserve and that
is this: “I ain’t as dumb as you look.

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:21.859
I ain’t as damn dumb as you look.

00:04:21.859 --> 00:04:29.789
We can keep talking but I want you to know
something, I ain’t as dumb as you look.”

00:04:29.789 --> 00:04:40.250
You know it’s interesting, once they see
that they know you are not playing checkers

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.930
in a chess game.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:43.620
You are playing chess.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:48.509
As long as we’re both playing chess, let’s
play.

00:04:48.509 --> 00:04:50.460
I got some damn moves too.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.300
Let’s just play.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:57.689
Don’t tell me how good a checker player
I am.

00:04:57.689 --> 00:05:03.090
That’s how I feel.

